'''Roganda Ismaren''' was an individual whose name was carved on the wall of a [[Mapuzo safehouse|safehouse]] on the [[planet]] [[Mapuzo]] that was part of the [[Hidden Path]], a network of safe houses that smuggled [[Force-sensitive]]s and [[Jedi]], safe from the [[Galactic Empire]] and to the planet [[Jabiim]] to get new identities and be protected. [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] saw their name among others on the wall when he and [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] were smuggled in by [[Tala Durith]].<ref name="Part III">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref> The same name was carved into a wall at the Path's base on [[Jabiim]].<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Roganda_Ismaren-crop.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Roganda Ismaren in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity]]
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Roganda Ismaren was introduced in "[[Part III]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', released on [[June 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="Part III" /> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], Roganda Ismaren first apppeared in [[Children of the Jedi (novel)|''Children of the Jedi'']], a [[1995]] novel by [[Barbara Hambly]].<ref name="COTJ">[[Children of the Jedi (novel)|''Children of the Jedi'']]</ref>

